00:10:26,484 --> 00:10:28,552
and it measures a much wider group

290
00:10:28,552 --> 00:10:30,186
than the bureau did.

291
00:10:30,450 --> 00:10:32,810
Why does the fee survive?

292
00:10:32,990 --> 00:10:35,040
Look at how it is built.

293
00:10:35,350 --> 00:10:37,190
It is a flat fee.

294
00:10:37,500 --> 00:10:39,620
At a bank like Wells Fargo,

295
00:10:39,620 --> 00:10:42,572
it is the same thirty-five dollars whether

296
00:10:42,572 --> 00:10:45,255
you overdraw by two dollars or by

297
00:10:45,255 --> 00:10:46,660
two hundred.

298
00:10:46,990 --> 00:10:48,283
On a small purchase,

299
00:10:48,283 --> 00:10:50,474
covered for a few days until the

300
00:10:50,474 --> 00:10:51,547
next deposit,

301
00:10:51,547 --> 00:10:53,900
that is a very wide margin.

302
00:10:54,100 --> 00:10:56,388
And without a federal cap,

303
00:10:56,388 --> 00:10:58,958
each bank still decides for itself what

304
00:10:58,958 --> 00:11:00,072
to charge.

305
00:11:00,317 --> 00:11:03,467
Let me draw the overdraft machine.

306
00:11:03,567 --> 00:11:04,468
On the left,

307
00:11:04,468 --> 00:11:06,917
a customer close to zero.

308
00:11:07,067 --> 00:11:08,220
In the middle,

309
00:11:08,220 --> 00:11:10,467
the bank paying a small purchase.

310
00:11:10,507 --> 00:11:11,422
On the right,

311
00:11:11,422 --> 00:11:12,102
the fee,

312
00:11:12,102 --> 00:11:15,047
coming back the moment the paycheck lands.

313
00:11:15,137 --> 00:11:16,441
Then the next month,

314
00:11:16,441 --> 00:11:18,011
the same customer,

315
00:11:18,011 --> 00:11:19,409
the same loop.

316
00:11:19,650 --> 00:11:21,863
So why do banks still make billions

317
00:11:21,863 --> 00:11:23,570
from overdrafts?

318
00:11:23,900 --> 00:11:24,977
Because the fee is small for most

319
00:11:24,977 --> 00:11:26,210
people and huge for a few.

320
00:11:26,210 --> 00:11:28,627
It is charged on tiny purchases,

321
00:11:28,627 --> 00:11:30,623
paid by customers who live close to

322
00:11:30,623 --> 00:11:31,266
zero,

323
00:11:31,266 --> 00:11:33,620
and repeated month after month.

324
00:11:33,620 --> 00:11:34,708
Banks cut it in half when the

325
00:11:34,708 --> 00:11:35,930
pressure was high.

326
00:11:36,140 --> 00:11:38,601
The cap that would have cut it

327
00:11:38,601 --> 00:11:40,940
again was erased.

328
00:11:40,940 --> 00:11:42,836
If you want to keep your money

329
00:11:42,836 --> 00:11:44,234
out of that machine,

330
00:11:44,234 --> 00:11:46,367
the simplest move is to check whether

331
00:11:46,367 --> 00:11:47,915
you opted in.

332
00:11:48,150 --> 00:11:50,781
Next time on The Hidden Economics,

333
00:11:50,781 --> 00:11:53,919
we follow the money behind another hidden

334
00:11:53,919 --> 00:11:56,430
link of the world economy.

335
00:11:56,430 --> 00:11:58,887
This is The Hidden Economics.
